# q79 Interface Contract

The q79 programs are concurrent external workers. This repository does not
inspect uncommitted working files for authority and never writes to those repos.

## Inputs accepted here

- Kernel-promoted q79 result identifiers;
- committed artifact hashes in `mtt-results-repro`;
- declared open blockers and guards; and
- stable typed interfaces published by the q79 workers.

## Outputs offered to q79

- a branch-independent repair object;
- a phase-retaining first-order operator contract;
- a central-extension representation candidate;
- a reduced list of bridge obligations; and
- no status promotion without q79-owner review.

## First future bridge

Given a promoted q79 endpoint `s_*`, construct a functor

```text
F_q79: NestedRepairStack -> q79CohesiveSource
```

and verify preservation of:

- the shared differential line and connection;
- the first-order deformation complex;
- the admissible fixed-symbol tangent and intrinsic Hessian;
- the inner curvature and outer repair-cost/Witten layers;
- the selected pairing and adjoint;
- the stratified tangent/normal structure;
- transferred products and the center/commutant count;
- the low-mode finite intertwiner; and
- all phase-sensitive data before squaring.

## H4-T5/H4-T6/H4-T7/H4-T8 interface reduction

The overlap mechanism itself is no longer part of the future bridge. H4-T5
proves that projective fundamental transitions with scalar triple cocycle glue
the curved endomorphism algebra and every strict-unital transferred operation
through `Ad(G_ij)`. This agrees with the committed q79 cohesive source and with
the hidden rank-nine to rank-80 adjoint cancellation used by the rank-102 Cech
compiler.

H4-T6 separately supplies the selected rational topology contraction on
`X=P_delta x S1_shared`. Its higher transfer is strict, so it cannot be used
to smuggle the auxiliary Heisenberg-Nil `m3` into the selected q79 topology.

H4-T7 removes initial unitarity as a primitive requirement. A bounded
domain-preserving chain/product transform supplies its own exact transported
metric. Comparison with the physical HYM metric is reduced to positive
metric-chain commutators and polar product defects, with explicit Hodge-error
bounds.

H4-T8 removes independently supplied nonlinear vertices from the interface.
The joint Taylor jet of the selected residual and endpoint-induced metric field
determines the repair Hessian and every higher repair vertex. After a reduced
Euclidean inverse is fixed, finite formal Wick weights follow functorially.
This is intrinsic to a physical residual on `X`; BHT is needed only when the
separate `J` presentation is also claimed to represent that endpoint.

The q79 worker now needs to export only endpoint-owned and analytic data that
this repository cannot select:

- the source hash and physical `V3/W9` Hermitian/HYM endpoint;
- the local transition, metric, connection, and domain arrays;
- the residual and metric-field jets at the selected endpoint;
- a bounded BHT/HYM realization joining the twisted coefficient source on `J`
  to the topology/carrier on `X`, only for a claimed presentation equivalence;
- its transported metric and physical mismatch operators, with certified
  H4-T7 chain/product defects or exact vanishing;
- the physical BV/BRST, causal inverse, state and renormalization data that do
  not follow from a positive repair cost;
- the intrinsic finite projector and reduced Green data; and
- the literal target map to the accepted 27-state algebra.

An ordinary commuting tensor factor is not an accepted substitute. The q79
ordinary-descent no-go forces the twisted/Morita formulation, and the 27-state
target must not be retyped as a rank-27 subspace of the rank-102 carrier.
